@q 6:12-13

@table
GST fact | Detail
In force | **1 July 2017** ("One Nation, One Tax")
Constitutional basis | **101st Amendment Act, 2016**; **Article 246A** (concurrent power), **269A** (IGST), **279A** (GST Council)
**GST Council** | Chaired by the **Union Finance Minister**; state finance ministers are members; decides rates, exemptions and thresholds by a **three-fourths** weighted vote (Centre one-third, states two-thirds)
Types | **CGST + SGST** (intra-state), **IGST** (inter-state and imports)
Kept outside GST | Alcohol for human consumption; petroleum crude, petrol, diesel, ATF and natural gas (until the Council decides)
**Revenue Neutral Rate** | Rate keeping revenue unchanged; **Arvind Subramanian** committee (2015) suggested about 15-15.5%
**Project Saksham** (2017) | New **IT network for indirect taxes** (CBIC)
**GST 2.0** (from **22 September 2025**) | Two main slabs, **5% and 18%**, plus **40%** on luxury and "sin" goods; the 12% and 28% slabs were removed
Collections | Over Rs. 1 lakh crore a month since October 2020; record of about **Rs. 2.37 lakh crore** (April 2025)
@end

**VAT stayed with the states** only for goods outside GST (petrol, alcohol), so the option "states may levy VAT if they so decide" was wrong in the 2016 question. UP's SGST collection is among the top five states.

