@q 6:66-70

@table
Direct tax (burden cannot be shifted) | Indirect tax (burden passed on to the buyer)
**Income tax**, **corporation tax** | **GST**, customs duty
Capital gains tax, securities transaction tax | Central excise (petroleum, tobacco)
Wealth tax (**abolished 2015-16**), gift tax (abolished 1998), estate duty (abolished 1985) | Earlier: sales tax/VAT, service tax, octroi, entertainment tax
**Progressive** (rate rises with income) | **Regressive** (same rate for rich and poor)
@end

Income tax was introduced by **James Wilson** in **1860**. **Nicholas Kaldor** proposed the **expenditure tax** (1956); it was levied from 1957. The **Direct Taxes Code** (2009-10) aimed to replace the Income-tax Act 1961; that finally happened through the **Income-tax Act, 2025**, effective **1 April 2026**. Under the new regime there is no tax on income up to **Rs. 12 lakh** (Budget 2025-26).

