@section 8.3 | Sources of Central Revenue and Who Levies What

@q 6:51-53

The **Central Sales Tax** (1956) was levied on **inter-state** sales and collected by the states; it did not apply to sales into **SEZs**. GST (IGST) has replaced it except for goods outside GST.

