@q 6:91-94

**Indira Vikas Patra** (bearer, no tax benefit) and **Kisan Vikas Patra** gave no income-tax rebate; NSC, PPF and ULIP did (under the old Section 80C). In a **PAN**, the 4th character shows the holder type: **P = individual**, C = company, H = HUF, F = firm, A = AOP, T = trust; the 5th is the first letter of the surname. A PAN card is proof of **identity and date of birth**, not address.

@q 6:75-76

@qnote 6:76 | When the question was asked, the gratuity ceiling was **Rs. 10 lakh** (option c); it rose to **Rs. 20 lakh** in March 2018 and to **Rs. 25 lakh** for Central government employees from 1 January 2024, so the source marks it (*).

The Supreme Court (October **2019**) upheld the Department of Telecommunications' wide definition of **Adjusted Gross Revenue**, which includes non-telecom income such as interest, dividends and forex gains, so telecom companies owed large dues.

